The API endpoint `{{baseUrl}}api/v1/menu/admin/add` is a POST request used to add a new menu item. The request should include a JSON payload in the raw request body type with the following parameters:

- `name` (string): The name of the menu item.

- `description` (string): Description of the menu item.

- `category` (string): Category of the menu item.

- `price` (number): Price of the menu item.


### Response

The response for this request is a JSON object with the following schema:

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "message": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "data": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "item": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "id": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "name": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "price": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "categoryID": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "updatedAt": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "createdAt": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```

The response data includes a boolean `status`, a string `message`, and a nested `data` object containing an `item` object with properties such as `id`, `name`, `description`, `price`, `categoryID`, `updatedAt`, and `createdAt`.

Additionally, related responses from other endpoints of the API return a list of menu items with similar data models, including `id`, `name`, `description`, `price`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `category` details.

The response returns a 200 status code upon successful execution.

